===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:suster|tree=1|text=:ine-pro}}

{{doublet|en|soror}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|sister}}, {{m|sco|syster||sister}}, {{cog|fy|sus}}, {{m|fy|suster||sister}}, {{cog|nl|zuster||sister}}, {{cog|de|Schwester||sister}}, {{cog|nb|søster||sister}}, {{cog|nn|-}} and {{cog|sv|syster||sister}}, {{cog|is|systir||sister}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍅𐌹𐍃𐍄𐌰𐍂||sister}}, {{cog|la|soror||sister}}, {{cog|ru|сестра́||sister}}, {{cog|lt|sesuo||sister}}, {{cog|sq|vajzë||girl, maiden}}, {{cog|sa|स्वसृ||sister|tr=svásṛ}}, {{cog|fa|خواهر||sister|tr=xâhar}}.

In standard English, the form with ''i'' is due to contamination with {{cog|non|systir||sister}}.

<!--Moved from [[sistren]].-->The plural ''[[sistren]]'' is from {{inh|en|enm|sistren}}, a variant plural of {{m|enm|sister}}, {{m|enm|suster|t=sister}}; compare {{m|en|brethren}}.

The sense for "{{taxfmt|Adelpha|genus}}-genus butterfly" is a {{semantic loan|nocap=1|en|mul|Adelpha}}, itself from {{cog|grc|ἀδελφή|t=sister}}.

