==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=brother of one's parent|:inh|enm:uncle<id:brother of one's parent>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|uncle}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|uncle}} and {{der|en|fro|oncle}}, from {{der|en|la-vul||*aunclum}}, from {{der|en|la|avunculus||maternal uncle|lit=little grandfather}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro||*h₂euh₂-n-tlo-|gloss=little grandfather}}, a dialectal diminutive of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂éwh₂os|*h₂éwh₂ō|grandfather, adult male relative other than one’s father}} (whence also {{m+|la|avus||grandfather}}). Displaced native Middle English {{m|enm|em||uncle}} from Old English {{m|ang|ēam||maternal uncle}}, containing the same Proto-Indo-European root, and Old English {{m|ang|fædera||paternal uncle}}. Compare {{cog|stq|Unkel||uncle}}, {{cog|nl|nonkel||uncle}}, {{cog|nds-de|Unkel||uncle}}, {{cog|de|Onkel||uncle}}, {{cog|da|onkel||uncle}}. More at {{l|en|eam}} and {{l|en|eame}}.

