# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To turn purple in colour.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966|author=James Workman|title=The Mad Emperor|publisher=Scripts|location=Melbourne, Sydney|page=143|passage=[T]he Capri cliffs, the tops of which were still pink against the '''purpling''' sky.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=David Edelstein|title={{w|In Nomine}}: Corporeal Player's Guide|publisher=Steve Jackson Games,|isbn=1-55634-389-2|page=8
|passage=The gang leader '''purpled''' and raised his gun.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To dye purple.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|volume=II|poem=The Day-Dream|section=The Sleeping Palace|page=152|passage=Year after year unto her feet, / She lying on her couch alone, / Across the '''purpled''' coverlet, / The maiden's jet-black hair has grown, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To clothe in purple.
# {{lb|en|US|informal|chiefly|in <<Christianity!Christian>>|_|summer camps}} To [[mingle]] with the opposite gender, especially in a flirtatious or amorous way. {{q|From the idea that mixing [[blue]], the color associated with boys, and [[pink]], the color associated with girls, makes purple.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author1=Cheryl Wylie-Harvey|author2=Jim Puyda|title=AJ and Friends: The Discovery|page=42|passage=“No '''purpling'''! No '''purpling'''!” Sarah shouted, and they all laughed. Robby and Amanda said boys were blue and girls were pink, and they didn't want those two colors mixing to make purple.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=K.E. Ganshert|title=The Gathering|
|text=“Cap doesn't like any '''purpling'''.” My brow furrows. “What is '''purpling'''?” “Boys are blue. Girls are red.” She threads her fingers together, so that her hands are linked as one and scrunches her nose again, like '''purpling''' is the last thing she'd ever want to do.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Dan Crabtree|title=A House Without Walls: How Christ Unites His Ethnically Divided Church|publisher=Ambassador International|isbn=9781649601711
|text=Summer’s Best Two Weeks is the name of a Christian summer camp in southwestern Pennsylvania {{...}}. Like anything involving coming-of-age adolescents, SB2W faced the challenge of how to motivate participation in their variety of activities beyond the uncomfortable promise of “'''purpling'''”—that is , boys and girls talking.}}
#* '''2023''' March 26, "No_Giraffe4124" (username), comment in "[https://www.reddit.com/r/summercamp/comments/122bbm7/campers_weed/ Campers & Weed?]" on ''Reddit'':
#*: [I worked at] a Christian camp. So obviously we have the "no '''purpling'''" rule. Kids still '''purpled''' behind our backs of course.

