Origin {{unc|en|nocap=1}}; perhaps from {{cog|nl|pinken|t=to blink}} or the English verb {{m|en|pink#Etymology 6|pink}} from the same source.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pink|v.2|144212|June 2006}}</ref> Perhaps from the notion of the petals being {{m|en|pink#Etymology 4|pinked}}. An earlier word for similar flesh-like colors, mostly displaced by ''pink'', was  {{m|en|incarnation}} ({{defdate|1300s}}; see {{w|Etymonline}}) and {{m|en|carnation}}. 

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|color}} A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|My new dress is a wonderful shade of '''pink'''.}}
#: {{color panel|pink|F52887}}
#: {{color panel|light pink|FF80BF}}
