#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ivan Hewett|title=Piano Man: a Life of John Ogdon by Charles Beauclerk, review: A new biography of the great British pianist whose own genius destroyed him &#91;print version: A colossus off-key, 10 May 2014, p.&nbsp;R27&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/books/bookreviews/10816279/Piano-Man-a-Life-of-John-Ogdon-by-Charles-Beauclerk-review.html|work={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Review)|date=11 May 2014|passage=The temptation is to regard him &#91;{{w|John Ogdon}}&#93; as an idiot savant, a big talent '''bottled''' inside a recalcitrant body and accompanied by a personality that seems not just unremarkable, but almost entirely blank.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251127195543/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/books/bookreviews/10816279/Piano-Man-a-Life-of-John-Ogdon-by-Charles-Beauclerk-review.html|archivedate=27 November 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|British}} To feed (an infant) [[baby formula]].
#: {{ux|en|Because of complications she can't breast feed her baby and so she '''bottles''' him.}}
# {{lb|en|British|slang}} To refrain from doing (something) at the last moment because of a sudden loss of courage.
#: {{ux|en|The rider '''bottled''' the big jump.}}
# {{lb|en|British|slang|sports}} To throw away a leading position.
#: {{ux|en|Arsenal '''bottled''' the Premier League.}}
# {{lb|en|British|slang}} To strike (someone) with a bottle.
#: {{ux|en|He was '''bottled''' at a nightclub and had to have facial surgery.}}
# {{lb|en|British|slang}} To [[pelt]] (a musical act on stage, etc.) with bottles as a sign of disapproval.
#: {{ux|en|[[w:Meat Loaf|Meat Loaf]] was once '''bottled''' at Reading Festival.}}
# {{lb|en|printing|intransitive}} Of pages printed several on a sheet: to rotate slightly when the sheet is folded two or more times.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Against the Clock|title=QuarkXPress 5: Advanced Electronic Documents|page=58
|passage=Closely related to creep is the process of '''bottling'''. As you may have noticed from your folded sheet of paper, pages don't merely creep when they're folded &mdash; they also rotate slightly. This rotation or '''''bottling''''' is caused by the thickness or bulk of the paper.}}

