==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|affrayed||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|'fraid||aphetic}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*preyH-}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:affraien|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|affrayed}}, {{m|enm|affraied}}, past participle of {{m|enm|afraien|t=to affray}}, from {{der|en|xno|afrayer|t=to terrify, disquiet, disturb}}, from {{der|en|fro|effreer}}, {{m|fro|esfreer|t=to disturb, remove the peace from}}, from {{pre|fro|es|t1=out|freer|t2=to secure, secure the peace|nocat=1}}, from {{der|en|frk|*friþu|t=security, peace}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*friþuz|t=peace}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*frijōną|t=to free; to love}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*prāy-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*prēy-|t=to like, love}}. {{surf|en|affray#Verb|-ed|nocat=1}}. Compare also {{m|en|afeard}}. More at {{m|en|free}}, {{m|en|friend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈfɹeɪd/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-afraid.ogg|a=US}}
** {{rhymes|en|eɪd|s=2}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈfɹɛd/|aa=Southern US|ref={{R:en:McDavid:1979|59|382}}}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}} {{tlb|en|predicative}}

# Impressed with [[fear]] or [[apprehension]]; in fear.
#: {{syn|en|afeared|alarmed|anxious|apprehensive|fearful|timid|timorous|Thesaurus:afraid}}
#: {{ux|en|He is '''afraid''' of death.}}
#: {{ux|en|He is '''afraid''' to [[ask out|ask her out]].}}
#: {{ux|en|He is '''afraid''' of the future.}}
#: {{ux|en|I’m not '''afraid''' of telling / to tell you the truth: I'm reluctant to go in you car because I’m too '''afraid''' of crashing.}}
#* {{quote-av
|en
|year=1964
|author=w:Harry S. Truman
|title=MP2002-77 Former President Truman Discusses Bigotry in the United States
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mdNJv4POFi0
|publisher=w:Harry S. Truman Presidential Library and Museum
|id=National Archives Identifier: [https://catalog.archives.gov/id/595162 595162]
|time=2:28
|text=I went through the worst Ku Klux proposition in the country at the time it was at its height. And I had to go down to the Ku Klux meeting and tell them what I thought of them, and I wasn't '''afraid''' of them at all. And I'm not '''afraid''' of this situation because I think it'll work out in a way that when these people sit down and get a chance to think and study the situation, they're going to be ashamed of some of the things they've done.}}
# [[regretful|Regretful]], [[sorry]]; expressing a [[reluctance]] to face an unpleasant situation. {{+obj|en|:that(clause)/clause|:so/:not}}
#: {{syn|en|sorry}}
#: {{ux|en|I am '''afraid''' I cannot help you in this matter.}}
#: {{ux|en|Need you bring him with you? -Yes, I'm '''afraid''' I must.}}
# [[worry|Worried]] about, feeling [[concern]] for, [[fear]]ing for (someone or something). {{+obj|en|:for}} <!-- https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/afraid%20for -->

====Usage notes====
* {{m|en|afraid|Afraid}} expresses a lesser degree of fear than {{m|en|terrified}} or {{m|en|frightened}}. It is often followed by the preposition {{m|en||of}} and the object of fear, or by an infinitive, or by a dependent clause, as shown in the examples above.

