==English==
{{wp}}
[[File:Banana Street Vendor Kenya.jpg|thumb|Bananas being sold by a street vendor in Kenya]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|bonana|bonano|bonanoe||all|_|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:bor|pt:banana|es:banana}}
{{bor+|en|pt|banana}} or {{bor|en|es|banana}}, derived from a {{der|en|nic|-}} language spoken in the [[Guinea]] region.<ref>{{R:OED Online|banana|pos=n|id=28257385}}</ref> Specific derivation is {{unc|en|unclear}}. Possible ancestor or cognate languages include {{der|en|wo|banaana}}, {{der|en|emk|banana}}, and {{der|en|vai|ꕒꘌꕯ}} or {{m|vai|ꕒꕌꕯ|tr=ɓaana}},<ref>{{R:MWO}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><ref>{{R:Collins}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|page=144|url=https://archive.org/details/outlinesofgramma00koeluoft|title=Outlines of a Grammar of the Vei Language: Together with a Vei-English Vocabulary|author=S.W. Koelle|publisher=London Church Missionary House|year=1854}}</ref> possibly from {{der|en|ar|بَنَان||fingertip, banana}}.<ref>Oxford Dictionaries citing John Ayto’s The Diner’s Dictionary: Word origins of food and drink [https://web.archive.org/web/20170710073834/http://blog.oxforddictionaries.com/2014/08/origin-banana/]</ref> However, ''Ay Baati Wolof'' (Munro & Gaye, 1997) posits that {{cog|wo|banaana}} is itself derived from {{cog|pt|banana}}.<ref>{{cite-book|en|title=Ay baati Wolof: A Wolof dictionary|author=Munro, Pamela|author2=Gaye, Dieynaba|year=1997|oclc=938011184|url=https://linguistics.ucla.edu/publications/opl_19.pdf|location=Los Angeles|series=
UCLA Occasional Papers in Linguistics|publisher=Department of Linguistics, University of California, Los Angeles|page=15}}</ref>

The racial slur derives from the notion that they are “[[yellow|Yellow]] (East-Asian) on the outside, but [[white|White]] (Westernized) on the inside”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈnɑːnə/|a=RP,SSB,Northern England,Wales}}
** {{audio|en|en-uk-banana.ogg}}
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈnænə/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-banana.ogg}}
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈnɐːnə/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈnanə/|a=Scotland}}
* {{hyph|en|ba|na|na}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːnə|ænə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q503}} The elongated curved tropical fruit of a {{vern|banana plant}}, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. {{defdate|from 1597}}
#: {{ux|en|Jimmy had a '''banana''' for breakfast.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author={{w|Sam Shepard}}|title=Spy of the First Person|chapter=27|url=|page=62|text=I'll need a few things. I'll need some mayonnaise and a silver tin of sardines, a '''banana'''. |isbn=9780525521563}}
## {{lb|en|North America|UK|Ireland}} In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana [[cultivar]], which may be eaten raw, as distinct from ''e.g.'' a [[plantain]] for cooking.
# The tropical tree-like plant which bears clusters of bananas, a plant of the genus ''[[Musa]]'' (but sometimes also including plants from {{taxfmt|Ensete|genus}}), which has large, elongated leaves. {{defdate|from 1697}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A yellow color, like that of a banana's skin. {{defdate|from 1923}}
#: {{color panel|FFE135}}
# {{lb|en|pejorative|ethnic slur}} A person of [[East Asian|East]] or [[Southeast Asian]] [[descent]], [[consider]]ed to be [[overly]] [[assimilated]] and [[subservient]] to [[white]] [[authority]]. {{defdate|from 1970}}
#: {{syn|en|Twinkie}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=[[wikipedia:Kelly Yang|Kelly Yang]]|title=Three Keys|page=24|passage=A '''banana''' was what Chinese people called a kid who had gotten too Americanized—yellow on the outside and white on the inside.}}
# {{lb|en|Malaysia|Singapore|Hong Kong|pejorative|ethnic slur}} A person of [[Chinese]] descent who cannot speak [[Mandarin]] or any Chinese [[dialect]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} The [[penis]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=_6cgAQAAMAAJ|title=Cop Feels of Three Men's "Privates"|author=Christopher Street|volume=10|text=The fact that the cop bought O'Brien a beer after feeling of his '''banana''' suggests that it must have been a promising one}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Sarah Miynowski|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=lg0mATRb6EAC&pg=PT36|title=Fishbowl|page=36|text=His you-know-what turned soft .. his eight o'clock class was the last thing on his mind five minutes ago, when his '''banana''' wasn't overripe.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Anthony Bunko|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=MdBxBAAAQBAJ&pg=PT71|title=Lord Forgive Me|page=71|text=Most of the gang were trying their best to shag the girls. One boy was sitting in a tree playing with himself and another was asking a table of teenagers if they would like to see his '''banana'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=4pQ4DwAAQBAJ&pg=PA234|title=Intimate Relationships in Cinema, Literature and Visual Culture|page=234|text=He adds that after eating his '''banana''' (sucking his penis), he wants anal sex, but she asks him to lick her pussy. Then he tells her no because it is disgusting.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[banana kick]].
# {{lb|en|nuclear physics}} A [[banana equivalent dose]].
# {{lb|en|computer science|colloquial}} A [[catamorphism]] (from the use of [[banana bracket]]s in the notation).
