===Etymology 1===
[[File:Crimson seedless on the vine.jpg|thumb|upright|A bunch of '''grapes''' ({{senseno|en|Q10978}})]]
{{ety|en|id=wine-berry|nodot=1|text=*|:inh|enm:grape<ety:bor<fro:grappe<t:cluster of fruit or flowers, bunch of grapes><ety:deverbal<graper<t:to pick grapes><lit:to hook><ety:bor<frk:*krappō<t:to hook><ety:der<ine-pro:<alt:*greb-><t:hook><unc><ety:from<*ger-<t:to turn, bend, twist>>>><ine-pro:<alt:*gremb-><unc><t:crooked, uneven><ety:from<*ger-<t:to turn, bend, twist>>>>>>>>>>>}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ger-|t=to turn, bend, twist}}. {{displaced|ang|wīnberġe|t=grape|lit=wine-berry}}. Cognate with {{cog|dum|krappe|t=hook}}, {{cog|goh|krapfo|t=hook}} (whence {{cog|de|Krapfen|t=Berliner doughnut}}. {{doublet|en|grappa}}. More at {{l|en|cramp}} and {{l|en|grapple|id=hook}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q10978}} {{lb|en|countable}} A small, round, smooth-skinned edible [[fruit]], usually purple, red, or green, that grows in [[bunch]]es on female vines of most species of genus {{taxfmt|Vitis|genus}} and the self-fertile plants of species {{taxfmt|Vitis vinifera|species}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''Grapes''' give us whole-fruit snacks, grape juice, raisins, wine, and more.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} Any woody [[vine]] of genus {{taxfmt|Vitis|genus}} that bears clusters of grapes; a [[grapevine]].
#: {{ux|en|wild '''grape''' covering the back slope}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any of various [[fruit]]s or [[plant]]s with varying resemblances to those of genus ''Vitis'' but belonging to other genera, not necessarily edible.
#: {{ux|en|sea '''grape'''; tail '''grape'''}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} A dark [[purple|purplish]]-[[red]] [[colour]], the colour of many grapes.
#: {{ux|en|For those seeking purply tones, the paint colors available include mauve, magenta, and '''grape'''.}}
#: {{color panel|6f2da8}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{clipping of|en|grapeshot}}.
#: {{ux|en|men mowed down by '''grape'''}}
#* {{RQ:Poe Pym|XX||pages=165{{ndash}}166|pageref=166|The boarding-nettings were up, the guns double-shotted with '''grape''' and canister, and the swivels loaded with canisters of musket-balls.}}
# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[mangy]] [[tumour]] on a [[horse]]'s [[leg]].
# {{lb|en|US|naval|_|slang}} A purple-shirted [[technician]] responsible for [[refuel]]ing [[aircraft]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1998|work=Approach|volume=43|issue=10|page=10|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=nT0w2bEwBDAC&pg=PA10|passage=I was horrified to see three '''grapes''' standing by the aircraft with the hose still connected.}}
# {{senseid|en|head}} {{lb|en|AAVE|slang}} A person's [[head]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:head}}

