salad.content:
==English==
{{wp}}
{{wikiquote}}
[[File:Salad platter.jpg|thumb|A salad.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|sallet}} {{defdate|16th|19th c.}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|sḗh₂l}}
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:salade|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|salade}}, from {{der|en|fro|salade}}, borrowed from Northern {{der|en|it|salada}}, ''[[salata]]'' (compare ''[[insalata]]''), from {{der|en|la-vul||*salāta}}, from {{m|la|*salāre}}, from {{der|en|la|saliō}}, from {{m|la|sal||salt}}. Vegetables were seasoned with brine or salty oil-and-vinegar dressings during Roman times.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|săʹləd}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsæləd/|a=RP,GA,CA,AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-salad.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsaləd/|a=SSB,Northern England,Scotland,Wales}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsælɪd/|a=Southern US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛləd/|a=NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|a=Indic|/ˈsaləɖ/|/səˈlɑɖ/|/səˈlɑd̪/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsælɪt/|a=obsolete|ref={{R:en:Grandgent:1899|238}} !!! {{R:en:Hall:1942|3|6|98}}}}
* {{rhymes|en|æləd|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q9266}}A food consisting principally of raw vegetables (especially [[greens#Noun|greens]], e.g. [[lettuce]]), other savoury ingredients (typically cooked), fruit, or confectionary; often involving two or more such ingredients mixed together, with larger items cut or torn into small pieces, and usually with a [[dressing]] or binding; usually served cold or at room temperature, as a dish or savoury sandwich filling.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|4|5|passage=''Lafeu''. ’Twas a good lady, ’twas a good lady: we may pick a thousand '''salads''' ere we light on such another herb.<br>''Clown''. Indeed, sir, she was the sweet marjoram of the '''salad''', or rather, the herb of grace.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author={{w|Harry E. Wedeck}}|title=Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs|publisher=The Citadel Press|location=New York|page=213|passage=At various times and in different areas '''salads''', compounded of meats, spices, tubers have been treated as of aphrodisiac value.}}
#: {{usex|en|We'd like a couple of cheese '''salads''' and two Pepsis, please.}}
# One or more raw [[vegetable]]s of the kind used in salads; typically greens (especially lettuce).
#: {{ux|en|sandwiches comprising a meat, a cheese, a '''salad''', and a condiment}}
#: {{usex|en|I prefer a bit of '''salad''' on my burger.}}
#: {{usex|en|Buy a bag of '''salad''' at the supermarket.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Any [[mixture]] of different things.
#: {{usex|en|word '''salad'''}} - incoherent speech
#* {{quote-web|en|date=Oct 16, 2021|author=Gurvinder Singh|title=Why Pakistan will fail|url=https://www.guruwonder.in/post/why-pakistan-will-fail|work=Guruwonder|passage=Rebuffed by the Arabs and then the Iranians for trying to be part of them and their societies, Pakistan is just a hotchpotch '''salad''' of people supposedly bound together by the myth of Muslim 'Ummah'.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231212230859/https://www.guruwonder.in/post/why-pakistan-will-fail|archivedate=12 December 2023}}

====Usage notes====
The word 'salad' is often preceded by the principal ingredient (e.g. 'potato salad', 'fruit salad') or a named type of salad (e.g. 'Waldorf salad'). When used alone, 'salad' usually implies the principal ingredient is lettuce or other greens.

