watermelon.content:
{{also|water melon}}
==English==
{{wp}}
[[File:Watermelons.jpg|thumb|Watermelons]]
{{wikidata lexeme|L208785}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|water|melon|etydate=1610s|tree=1}}

{{com|en|water|melon|type=endo}}. Compare {{cog|fr|melon d'eau}}, {{cog|de|Wassermelone}}{{,}} and {{cog|es|melón de agua}}.

The meanings referring to environmentalists and behind-schedule projects derive from the idea of having a [[green]] (eco-friendly, on-schedule) outward appearance while being [[red]] (socialist, behind schedule) in a hidden way comparable to that of the fruit.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɔːtəˌmɛlən/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɑtəɹˌmɛlən/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɒːt̞ɚˌmɛlən/|a=IE}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈwaːhɐˌmɛlən/|/ˈwaːʔɐˌmɛlən/|/ˈwaːʔɚˌmɛlən/|a=Dublin}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈwɔːɾɚˌmɛlən/|a=Ulster}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-watermelon.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|wa|ter|mel|on}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q17507129}}A plant of the species {{taxfmt|Citrullus lanatus|species}}, bearing a [[melon]]-like fruit.
# {{senseid|en|Q38645}}The fruit of the watermelon plant, having a green rind and watery flesh that is typically bright red when ripe and contains black [[seed]]s.
# {{lb|en|pejorative|slang}} An [[environmentalist]] with [[socialist]] leanings, an [[ecosocialist]].
#* {{RQ:Observer|author=Robin McKie|title=Merchants of Doubt by Naomi Oreskes and Erik M Conway|date=2010-08-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2010/aug/08/merchants-of-doubt-oreskes-conway|passage=According to this distorted view of life, environmentalists are '''watermelons''' – green on the outside, red on the inside – who want to impose regulation, “the slippery slope to socialism”, on the use of tobacco, ozone-destroying chemicals and greenhouse gases.|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/M87vy|archivedate=16 July 2025}}
# {{senseid|en|Q24820286}} A [[pinkish]]-red [[colour]], like that of watermelon flesh (also called watermelon pink).
#: {{color panel|FDBCB4}}
# A project that is [[present]]ed as on [[schedule]] when it actually has parts that are [[fall behind|falling behind]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://dzone.com/articles/watermelon-reporting|work=DZone|passage=The nuts and bolts of any project are transparency. If the project status is transparent, the '''watermelons''' can’t arise. If anybody is able to get the information, it will be difficult to hide something.|title='''Watermelon''' Reporting|date=2011-08-08|author=Marc Löffler|publisher=AnswerHub|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260829023438/https://dzone.com/articles/watermelon-reporting|archivedate=29 August 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/watch-out-watermelons-project-reports-ken-burrell|work=LinkedIn|passage=As a PMO [project management officer], wherever I see '''watermelon''' reporting, I encourage the PM [project manager] to be brave and honest enough to ask for help.|title=Watch out for '''watermelons''' in project reports|date=2015-09-17|author=Ken Burrell|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260918163234/https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/watch-out-watermelons-project-reports-ken-burrell|archivedate=18 September 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.cio.com/article/3617909/combatting-the-watermelon-effect-to-improve-digital-experience.html|work=CIO|passage=[see title]|title=Combatting the '''Watermelon''' Effect to Improve Digital Experience|date=2021-04-24|author=Sumir Karayi|publisher=IDG Communications|accessdate=5 June 2021|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210605175839/https://www.cio.com/article/3617909/combatting-the-watermelon-effect-to-improve-digital-experience.html|archivedate=5 June 2021}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|slang}} A [[breast]], especially that of an [[adult]] or [[adolescent]] [[female]] [[human]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:breasts}}

