# Without [[use]] or the [[possibility]] to be used.
#: {{syn|en|unusable|unutilizable}}
#: {{ux|en|This fork's prongs are bent. It's '''useless''' now.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 June 30|author=Philip Haigh|title=Regional trains squeezed as ECML congestion heads north|journal=RAIL|issue=934|page=53|text=I'm all for opening new stations (Transport Scotland is planning another at East Linton, about halfway between Drem and Dunbar), but they are '''useless''' without a decent service.}}
# [[unhelpful|Unhelpful]], not [[useful]]; [[pointless]] (of an action).
#: {{syn|en|void}}
#: {{ux|en|I think it's '''useless''' to keep this discussion going. It's like talking to a brick wall.}}
#: {{ux|en|I tried my best to make him quit smoking, but my efforts were '''useless'''. He now smokes six packs a day.}}
# {{lb|en|pejorative|of a person}} [[good-for-nothing|Good-for-nothing]]; not [[dependable]].
#: {{ux|en|Bill never mows the lawn, takes out the trash or anything. He's '''useless''', but I love him anyways.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|somewhat|derogatory}} Of a person, [[unable|Unable]] to [[do]] [[well]] at a particular [[task]] or [[endeavor]].
#: {{ux|en|My brother is '''useless''' at most computer games, but he is an awesome PS2 player.}}
#: {{ux|en|Why do you keep trying? You're obviously '''useless''' at it.}}

====Synonyms====
