====Usage notes====
* In a more generic sense, like when used as an ingredient, ''juice'' is usually instead called {{m|sv|saft}}.
* Juice always refers to a beverage containing 100% fruit. Fruit beverages with added sugar and/or water are called {{m|sv|saft}}.
* A well-known, largely unsuccessful attempt was made to popularize "{{l|sv|jos}}" as a Swedified spelling in the 1970s. "Jos" is now often used in tongue-in-cheek reference.

